<!--/Post: 13302-->
<!--Post: 13304--><!--Time: 1114845259-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13304"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 30, 2005 - 12:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is only partly related. I was just reading this article at KAKE - <a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1524417.html">Terrorized By Dennis Rader?</a> <BR> <BR>And the following floored me: <BR> <BR><i>&#34;...King, who has worked for the same doctor for 10 years, says she started taking things very seriously when she says she caught Rader window peeping. Again, she called police. <BR> <BR>“And, they said, ‘Mamm, there is a difference between looking in windows and walking by windows,’” says King. “I’m like, ‘Well, I think you know when someone steps in front of your windows.’”</i> <BR> <BR>Even with Denny the Deadly Peeping Dog Catcher in the clink, is there something basically rotten in bucolic Park City Government, <i>still?</i> <BR> <BR>This woman has a helluva lawsuit on her hands if she&#39;s telling the truth.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13304-->
<!--Post: 13305--><!--Time: 1114864743-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13305"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 30, 2005 - 5:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve: and DTDC&#39;s boss keeps trying to justify this behavior because she had code violations. There is no excuse for this behavior! The recently elected mayor seems to be putting forth the effort to correct this within the compliance department. I think the mayor needs to start by firing Denny&#39;s boss.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13305-->
<!--Post: 13310--><!--Time: 1114866577-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13310"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 30, 2005 - 6:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rader&#39;s job did not give him any privilege to trample on the Constitutional rights of others. Park City should be taken to task for allowing him to run amuck. Looking at Rader&#39;s home at the time of his arrest is a good indicator of a double standard! His place looked like crap. Physician, heal theyself. <BR> <BR>Park City better have lots of lawsuit monies. They are going to need it. It leads one to speculate what else in the way of city scandals they are sweeping under the rug. Perhaps they were scared to death of Rader.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13310-->
<!--Post: 13320--><!--Time: 1114972434-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13320"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 01, 2005 - 11:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know what you mean about his place. Looked kinda junked up to me. Not that I can necessarily talk all the time about such a thing, but I do have small children as an excuse. <BR> <BR>I will say this one positive thing for DTDC; he had great taste in mini-vans. &#42;snicker&#42; <BR> <BR><i>&#40;to rob the joke, I drive a very, very similar make and model to his Pontiac Montana.&#41;</i><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13320-->
<!--Post: 13328--><!--Time: 1115044705-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13328"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 02, 2005 - 7:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->LAW SUIT LAW SUIT LAW SUIT <BR>Park City DESERVES to have law suits brought against them....it is riduculous, frightening and pathetic what the citizens had to tolerate and put up with with BTK as their COMPLIANCE Officer.  SO many lives taken, so many lives uprooted and Park City STILL maintains that the Demon A&#42;&#42; was JUST DOING HIS JOB.... <BR>was Stalking and Harassment part of his job description?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13328-->
<!--Post: 13329--><!--Time: 1115059912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13329"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 02, 2005 - 11:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky - hey how is YOUR Spring time going?  I broke my foot so I was off for three days...hobbling...the demon a&#42;&#42; will be giving his pleas tomorrow.  It is tomorrow right?  <BR>I am astounded that someone could even consisder being a &#34;pen pal&#34; to a serial killer...ANY killer for that matter. <BR>How can she even stand to TOUCH his letters.  <BR>I am praying that soon justice will be served on this deadly monster demon a&#42;&#42;- <BR>and also, I hope your father is doing well.  And I hope Park City Officials have SURELY learned some sort of lesson here.... <BR>I&#39;m venting<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13329-->
<!--Post: 13339--><!--Time: 1115104010-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13339"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 12:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OK, I&#39;ll play devil&#39;s advocate.  Suppose Rader has Multiple Personality Disorder.  &#40;I know, I know it&#39;s Dissociative Identity Disorder now&#41; <BR> <BR>Then all the people who say they never saw the monstrous side aren&#39;t stupid, they&#39;re right.  And they&#39;re defense witnesses on the insanity issue. <BR> <BR>The confession doesn&#39;t touch the defense because: <BR> <BR>ta da:  it wasn&#39;t him confessing, it was an alter. <BR> <BR>In an odd way his Christian role and his BTK role are classic Jeykle and Hyde. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s also a perfect insanity defense. <BR> <BR>Phoenix <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13339-->
<!--Post: 13344--><!--Time: 1115122350-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13344"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 5:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It will never wash. I can&#39;t think of a case offhand where anyone has made it stick. Kenneth Bianchi, one of the Hillside Stranglers, tried, and almost succeeded, until someone figured out that he was faking his hypnosis sessions.  <BR> <BR>I do think there is an instability in his core identity, but don&#39;t know if it qualifies as D.I.D., exactly. I say this if for no other reason than the way his photos seem to shift over the years... he never looks the same in two photos. That&#39;s a bizarre quality that not everyone has. His handwriting, slanting this way and that, also may affect this unstable, shifting persona. But I doubt it adds up to actual D.I.D. There&#39;s a big debate going on in the world of psychology/psychiatry as to whether D.I.D. even exists, stories as fundamental as that of &#34;Sybil&#34; being called into question as to how truly they were told.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13344-->
<!--Post: 13345--><!--Time: 1115125469-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13345"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 6:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, I have noticed this too. Looking at his pics, you would never guess this was the same man. <BR>The high school pics have no resemblance to the air force pics, air force pics have no resemblance to the ADT pics, even the chubby faced happy park city dog catcher pic looks like another person. Then seeing him in court at the prelim, I was floored at his appearance. If I didnt know better, I wouldnt believe it was him. <BR> <BR>About the handwriting, I now believe Sonya Gray&#39;s <BR>story, she confirmed it to one of the local newstations, and looking at that handwriting <BR>is incredible. I think on 1-15-05 he was ready to kill again.   <BR> <BR>Ask me what I think he was doing on  <BR>Dec 8 2004, if you dare.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13345-->
<!--Post: 13348--><!--Time: 1115131649-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13348"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 7:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty - tell us...what WAS he doing on 12/8/2004?  I also am blown away about the difference&#39;s in his pic&#39;s...he changes all the time.  I would really like to know what the &#34;wife&#34;&#39;s life was like with him...I wonder - same thing?  Different man every day?  His photo&#39;s all shift... <BR>ALso Itty where can I find the Sonya Gray story? <BR>Thanks. <BR>The s.o.b. plead not guilty. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13348-->
<!--Post: 13397--><!--Time: 1115214108-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13397"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 6:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->12-8-2004 <BR>Summer Shipp, last seen &#34;independence&#34; MO, door to door survey taker. Car found with purse locked inside. not exactly sure on the dates, but about 7 weeks later, her grocery store card was turned in at store and mailed to her house. She lived in the &#34;valentine&#34; neighborhood. Even more time goes by and her daughter gets a search together to look for clues, and they found another shopping card, in a place previously searched. <BR> <BR>From the beginning, I had a feeling about this case. Valentine neighborhood, red heart on cereal box, what looked like a rose stem sticking out of the box. 12-8 date. Not much to go on, but the double letters in her name. <BR> <BR>Then the cards start showing up. <BR> <BR>The website is &#34;<a href="http://www.friendsofsummer.com" target=_top>www.friendsofsummer.com</a>&#34; to look at all the news articles, and see what her daughter has planned. <BR> <BR>I may be crazy, but I think it should be looked into. <BR> <BR>Else, I cant find the Sonya Gray story now. I know I read it, pretty recently, that another news agency contacted her to verify her story, and she stuck with it. If he was stalking her on 1-15, maybe he was busy on 12-8 in independence. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13397-->
<!--Post: 13410--><!--Time: 1115222695-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13410"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 9:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Else, here is KAKE&#39;s story on S. Gray <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1372967.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1372967.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13410-->
<!--Post: 13411--><!--Time: 1115224547-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13411"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 9:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yea! Thanks Itty!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13411-->
<!--Post: 13517--><!--Time: 1115439788-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13517"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 9:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rude finger down the throat of reality: <BR> <BR>Verdicts are based on evidence not facts.  An expert opinion is evidence.  In a court room the defendant&#39;s mental state is whatever the expert witness can convince a jury that it is. <BR> <BR>If the defense can get one psychologist to say he suffers from DID it becomes a jury issue. <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13517-->
